# mm.camera.preview

Portable processing and button debounce for the PICO-Cam-A preview. The fixed
324x244 grayscale input maps to a 240x135 image using nearest sampling,
fractional area averaging, or area averaging with temporal history. Button
state accepts one falling edge or low level after 30 ms of observed release,
including taps latched while capture blocks and unsigned timer wraparound.

The caller owns frame, image and button state. It resets temporal history on
restart or a mode change. The module does not access hardware or configure
sensor exposure. Output coordinates passed to sample must be in range.

Written for modules.cpp, not copied from ArduCAM or Waveshare. Host regression
coverage lives in tests/mm/camera/preview/ and uses the normal mm.test runner:

```sh
sh test.sh --host tests/mm/camera/preview/
```
